This study addresses the estimation of functions within the Hankel Sobolev space $H^{
u}_{\mathbb{S}}$ using circular prolate spheroidal wave functions (PSEs). We demonstrate that for $
u \geq 0$, the orthonormal basis formed by PSEs offers a superior alternative to the standard basis derived from Bessel functions of the first kind of order $
u$. Furthermore, we establish a new inequality regarding the reconstruction of functions in $H^{
u}_{\mathbb{S}}$ via PSE series, which yields a more favorable constant than the bound provided by the Bessel series expansion.
